    22	# Design analysis for combo D4/2 + D5/0
    23	# --------------------------------------
    24	# 1. Concrete behavior and trace:
    25	#    - Original dbff022c assumes a hollow sprite uses one border color, so one hole is
    26	#      solved by counting adjacent border cells and then solid-filling the hole.
    27	#    - This combo breaks both assumptions at once:
    28	#      a) one sprite border uses two visible colors, `major` and `accent`;
    29	#      b) output holes are striped, not solid.
    30	#    - Example on one 5x4 ring:
    31	#      the hole-adjacent shell cells may contain accent=4 and major=2 in a 4:2 split,
    32	#      while the full shell contains major=2 and accent=4 in an 8:4 split.
    33	#      Original logic would key the palette with 4 and flood-fill every hole cell.
    34	#      Combo logic must key the palette with 2, then paint alternating stripes with
    35	#      mapping[2] and background 0.
    36	#    - Therefore the fusion is not a loose concatenation: the lookup step must read the
    37	#      whole shell before the stripe writer runs, otherwise the wrong palette key is chosen.
    38	# 2. Complexity calibration:
    39	#    - Borders use exactly two colors. That is enough to make "local vote vs global
    40	#      majority" visible without turning shells into noise.
    41	#    - Stripe orientation has only two cases, derived from the hole bbox:
    42	#      wider-or-square holes -> vertical stripes, taller holes -> horizontal stripes.
    43	#    - Filled sprites are generated so both the majority conflict and stripe visibility
    44	#      happen often; otherwise the task would collapse back toward the source task.
    45	# 3. Implicit-assumption audit against the original main():
    46	#    - `_best_palette` and `_palette_mapping` only depend on the edge legend geometry and
    47	#      uniqueness of palette keys, so they remain valid.
    48	#    - The original hole filler assumed one adjacent color represented the whole sprite.
    49	#      That fails for multicolor shells, so the solver now labels full non-palette
    50	#      connected components and counts colors over the entire touching component.
    51	#    - The original writer could mutate every hole cell to one color. That fails for
    52	#      striped interiors, so the solver must enumerate all bg holes before any writeback,
    53	#      then paint each hole by row/column parity inside its own bbox.
    54	# 4. Placement legality:
    55	#    - The generator keeps palette and sprites separated by at least one background cell.
    56	#    - Every filled sprite has exactly one enclosed hole with area >= 2, so stripes are
    57	#      visible and holes never merge with the outer background.
    58	#    - The multicolor border constructor guarantees `major` is the strict whole-shell
